{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Rage Gene|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Gnar
|skill        = I
|icon         = Rage Gene.png
|blurbicon    = Rage Gene.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Innate - Rage Gene:}} {{ci|Gnar|Mini Gnar}} generates ''Rage'' while fighting. At maximum ''Rage'', his next {{tip|ability}} will be ''{{cis|Mega Gnar}}'' as he transforms, losing ''Mini Gnar's'' passive effects in exchange for increased stats and new abilities.
|blurb2       = ''Mega Gnar'' form lasts for some time before reverting to ''Mini Gnar'', afterwards he cannot generate ''Rage'' for some time.
|description  = {{sbc|Innate - Rage Gene:}} {{ci|Gnar|Mini Gnar}} generates {{pp|4;7;11|1 to 11}} ''{{ai|Rage Gene|Gnar|Rage}}'' over 2 seconds upon dealing or receiving damage, up to 100. Against non-champions, {{tip|basic attacks}} {{tip|on-hit}} and ''{{ai|Boomerang Throw|Gnar}}'' instantly generate{{ft|{{pp|4*0.125;7*0.125;11*0.125|1 to 11|round=false}} ''Rage''.|{{fd|12.5%}} of the amount.}} Against champions, ''{{ai|Boomerang Throw|Gnar}}'' instantly generates{{ft|{{pp|4*0.25;7*0.25;11*0.25|1 to 11|round=false}} ''Rage'',|25% of the amount,}}and basic attacks ''on-hit'' instantly generate{{ft|{{pp|4*0.5;7*0.5;11*0.5|1 to 11|round=false}}.|50% of the amount.}}''{{ai|Boomerang Throw|Gnar}}'' can only generate ''Rage'' once per cast, and grants ''Rage'' based on the first enemy hit. '''Gnar's''' ''Rage'' decays after being [[combat status|out of combat]] for 13 seconds.
|icon2        = Rage Gene 2.png
|description2 = At maximum ''Rage'', '''Gnar's''' {{tip|abilities}} switch to {{cis|Mega Gnar}} abilities, for 4 seconds and until transforming back to his ''Mini Gnar'' form, with the exception of ''{{ai|Hop and Crunch|Gnar|Hop}}'', which switches after the transformation. Casting any of them during this time also causes '''Gnar''' to transform into {{ci|Mega Gnar}} instantly, else he will transform automatically after the 4 seconds have elapsed.
|description3 = '''Gnar's''' {{ci|Mega Gnar|Mega}} form lasts for 15 seconds, with his ''Rage'' bar depleting as an indication of remaining time. ''Rage cannot be generated while in this form.'' Afterwards, '''Gnar''' returns to {{ci|Gnar|Mini Gnar}}, retaining his {{sti|health|{{as|'''current''' percentage health}}}} and becoming too [[File:Rage Gene 4.png|20px]] ''tired'' to generate ''Rage'' for 15 seconds. 
|description4 = '''Gnar''' gains different stat bonuses based on whether he is in ''{{ai|Mini Gnar|Gnar|Mini}}'' or ''{{ai|Mega Gnar|Gnar|Mega}}'' form. Both of '''Gnar's''' forms share their ability cooldowns. 
|targeting    = Passive
|affects      = Self
|damagetype   = 
|spellshield  = 
|spelleffects = 
|projectile   = 
|grounded     = 
|knockdown    = 
|notes        = 
* The ''Rage'' generated upon dealing or receiving damage occurs over 2 seconds with 4 ticks every {{fd|0.5}} seconds. It also does not stack but instead refreshes with subsequent applications (of dealing or receiving damage).
* In-game, the value on the ''Rage'' bar always displays rounded down to the nearest integer.
* {{cis|Mega Gnar}} gained health is not affected by {{tip|healing}} modifiers such as {{tip|Grievous Wounds}} and those from [[item]]s and [[rune]]s.
* When returning to {{ci|Gnar|Mini Gnar}}, '''Gnar''' will only retain his current health percentage, not current health total.
* '''Gnar's''' abilities share {{sti|cooldowns}} across forms.
* The ''Rage'' bar is <span style="color:white">'''white'''</span> when under 60 range, <span style="color:yellow">'''yellow'''</span> when equal to or above 60 rage, and <span style="color:red">'''red'''</span> at 100 rage.
* If '''Gnar''' transforms into {{ci|Mega Gnar}} while on enemy's sight and later goes back to {{ai|Mini Gnar|Gnar|Mini}} while on the fog of war, enemies will see {{cis|Mega Gnar}} icon both in the scoreboard and minimap, even if they regain vision of '''Gnar'''. This will stay this way until '''Gnar's''' {{ci|Mega Gnar|Mega}} form ends while on enemy's sight.{{bug}}
|flavorsound = {{sm2|Gnar_Original_Transform_2.ogg}} ''"GNAR!"''
}}
